  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Creator, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>One essential condition for creation is freedom. As such, Creators are some of the freest spirits around. They are particularly independent in 2 specific ways: mentally and externally.</p>
              <p>Externally, Creators aim to have secure finances and the <span class="text-orange">ability to truly live their passions</span> without anyone dictating over them. As such, you are thrifty yet have lots of savings to show for your work. You live below your means, act below your means, and often thrive as a result.</p>
              <p>Mentally, you are unbound by anything. You will explore even the corners that most people would say are forbidden. This is because you are aware that goodness exists outside the box and that the only thing you really have to do is find it. With this mindset, you will consequently be independent enough to do things differently. </p>
              <p>Creators need a drive in order to make things happen. Luckily, this is something that you aren’t lacking. Your purpose in life not only serves as your <span class="text-orange">overwhelming driving force</span>, but it’s also limitless and is a reliable fallback when all else fails.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>This means that when the going gets tough, you won’t just lie down and quit. You’ll actually get your act together and figure out the best possible solution for the crisis. Since you are dedicated to your work, it naturally means that people around you will see you as a source of strength.</p>
          <p>Lastly, it’s also the very thing that drives you to explore multiple solutions. The fact that you have a purpose ultimately means that you will feel safe exploring things and constantly finding new ways to make life amazing and interesting for you. In other words, your purpose effectively primes you for expansion, and you should revel in it.</p>
          <p>In the pursuit of creation, doing the maximal amount of work for the least amount of resources is most often optimal. This allows you to focus on other aspects of your life.</p>
          <p>As a Creator, it’s naturally expected that you are an efficient worker. When you create, you don’t just let yourself and your mind go; you actually conserve some much-needed energy and time to make sure you are able to get around everything you want to do-- hobbies or extra work alike.</p>
          <p>And even if it’s not deliberate at times, your rational personality knows for a fact that efficiency and optimization are two of creation’s greatest traits. In other words, you don’t just create what you want: you create something that’s fundamentally useful to yourself and other people. This allows you to have <span class="text-orange">the mind of an inventor</span>-- endlessly curious but always keeping yourself in check.</p>
          <p>As a creative personality, you are often feeling so many emotions at once. With each emotion felt, you are able to view reality from multiple perspectives. Ironically enough, despite the harrowing experience, this might provide you at times, it makes you more capable of empathy than most.</p>
          <p>This is because you are more capable of putting yourself in everybody’s shoes at some point. This works, for example, in the workplace, where you’re surrounded by people who each have their own quirks and emotions for the day. You are able to feel their sadness, joy, and even pain.</p>
          <p>Of course, this naturally makes you more capable of giving them encouragement when they feel down and amplifying the positive emotions they might feel due to your actions. Since you are a Creator, you will often give them encouragement in unconventional ways. You may, for example, give someone your artwork or pay for parties-- you may do things out of your way just to show that you care. Indeed, you have your own brand of <span class="text-orange">kindness and emotional intelligence</span>.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Creator, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your calm nature, you often feel emotionally certain and secure. Whereas other archetypes tend to be turbulent and unsure, you are inclined to focus on stability and honesty. </p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, this tendency will bring balance. As such, you may have a tendency to look for a person who naturally embodies this honest attitude as well. This is because a relationship cannot work if there is no honesty between the two parties.</p>
              <p>Given this, you are likely to look at love from the <span class="text-orange">perspective of truth</span>. If I am telling the truth, is the one I’m with also doing the same? How can I trust my romantic partner and know that they’re holding up their end of the bargain?</p>
              <p>One could very well point out that a potential problem of your romantic relationships is the element of suspicion. With all these questions swirling in your head, it would seem as though you are in a <span class="text-orange">perpetual state of flux</span>, constantly worrying about whether or not your partner is faithful.</p>
              <p>However, this is actually untrue because you are also calm. In other words, since you are sure about your feelings with other people, you are also sure about who to trust and who to give those feelings to.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>As such, your romantic setup might very well be one of the most stable on this front out of all the other archetypes. Before you engage in a relationship, you critically evaluate it, and at the point, you are able to confess, it means that your relationship will work.</p>
          <p>Thus, you should only work on making sure that you continue having this sort of attitude. Although the world can have terrible surprises at times, the reality is that honesty is an essential component of a relationship that should never be done away with. You need to be the model in this case-- the first person to actually make an honest move-- and encourage your romantic partner to follow suit. By doing so, stability will surely follow.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Looking at the core qualities of your archetype, we’ll see a Creator who <span class="text-orange">seeks nothing less than love in its absolute, most perfect form</span>. You are likely to try and tailor it to your image of perfection, and will therefore be a dominant personality.</p>
          <p>This trait often manifests in your likelihood to look for a romantic setup that actually caters to this desire. When you find the right person, you will often convince them to do this for you, not necessarily for your own personal sake (such as money, etc), but you may think of trying to make sure that everything is perfect.</p>
          <p>On the one hand, this is a perfectly understandable thing for a Creator to do. After all, although nothing is truly perfect, you can in fact find the right person whom you’d love to spend the rest of your life with. Seeking to expedite this by making sure that everything is perfect is almost necessary to make this pipedream come true.</p>
          <p>However, this can also make your relationship difficult to navigate. The fact of the matter is that while one can empathize with your dream of love, no one likes being told what to do-- especially if you’re dating a person with a similar archetype. In your case, therefore, there might be disagreements between you two about your relationship arrangements.</p>
          <p>This disagreement, if handled poorly, might prove fatal to your relationship in the long run, as the two of you will likely be fighting for control over who gets to set the relationship’s theme.</p>
          <p>To avoid this unfortunate scenario, therefore, you should avoid trying to completely dominate the relationship. Instead, you should <span class="text-orange">seek compromise</span> in order to make sure that everything is in perfect order. The relationship can and will work, but only if you are willing to find common ground with your partner. Once this is settled, love will blossom.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Creator is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Creator</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Creator is a combination of introversion, egocentrism, rationality, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to engineering, software development, and industrial design. With their creative nature, Creators will undoubtedly find themselves at home with these jobs. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/civil-engineer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Civil Engineer</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Creators are best suited as builders. Because they have the natural knack to create useful things, they’ll find it natural to build things that are useful to everyone. </p>
              <p>As a civil engineer, your primary task will be to enhance public infrastructure: roads, bridges, train stations-- anything that the public itself could peruse will be under your effective supervision. This is a great opportunity for you because it will put your creative capacity to its limits: when building new things, you have to integrate both utility and elegance, ensuring some real intellectual challenge.</p>
              <p>One other trait that will benefit you in this enterprise is your efficiency. As a general rule, everything that you build should not just be grand: it should be as cost-effective as possible. Consequently, this will allow you to create efficient designs, and when combined further with a supreme work ethic, nothing can stop you from performing your task.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>In addition to its positive traits, being a civil engineer also allows you to mitigate some other traits. For one, it helps you exploit your cautiousness to its fullest extent. While overcautiousness can be a bad thing, in this case, it’s actually very helpful since civil engineering is something that can take lives and livelihoods away from other people when done wrong. Your meticulousness will undoubtedly help you here.</p>
          <p>Another thing this job will undoubtedly temper is your own tendency to be misunderstood. Being a civil engineer means making sure that everything is accurate and to the point, and as such, it will force you to not only be innovative but also articulate in your own explanations. This will naturally ensure that people will understand you at all times.</p>
          <p>With all these strengths, it’s easy to see why this is a good job for you. Being a Creator with the given purpose of actually ensuring that people’s lives will be better will undoubtedly strengthen your own belief in yourself-- whatever insecurities you have will be put to rest once you see the progress in everything that you do. Indeed, by being a Civil Engineer, you will be happy for a long time.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/software-developer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>App/Software Developer</h5>
              <p>Since the advent of the internet and the advancement of technology, creation has walked a different route. No longer were we exclusively creating things that were tangible; we’re also creating things in the virtual world, and these things have actual uses to people.</p>
              <p>Naturally, as a Creator, this makes app and software development a perfect fit for you. With the ability to create virtual tools, you will be in a unique position where you could potentially shape the way other people experience their lives. Be it creating a food service app or even video games, there’s always something to do in this industry.</p>
              <p>Aside from that, you naturally have the option of working alone or with a team. If you choose to work alone, you’ll have the creative freedom to create whatever app suits your sensibilities. By then, it will only be a matter of time before you can create something truly different.</p>
              <p>However, the true beauty of this industry comes from the ability to actually have a team behind you. There is nothing more joyful than seeing your collective vision clash and finally come together as a magnificent piece of art that will revolutionize the way other people think.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Naturally, should you choose to work in a team setup, this particular field will help you overcome your being opinionated, because working with a team will allow you to realize that there are always multiple opinions on how to improve something, and that it is fundamentally better to bring things together.</p>
          <p>With each app or software you create, you will naturally make people’s lives easier and happier. As such, there is no doubt that you will thrive in an industry that effectively primes you for it.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/industrial-designer.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Industrial Designer</h5>
              <p>Creation is the ultimate method that humanity uses to constantly improve its state. With every era, we become better at not only prolonging our lives or perpetuating peace, but also indulging ourselves. An industry that naturally paves the way for all three of these is industrial design-- an easy pick for the Creator archetype.</p>
              <p>As a Creator, you will often be in the thick of mass production and invention. Where there is something that is worth inventing, you are often the brains behind it. You are responsible for creating some of the most convenient technologies that continue to make humanity better-- be it the cellphone or even the most high-tech sports car.</p>
              <p>With the amount of freedom often afforded to these gems of humanity, you are guaranteed to be a powerhouse that people won’t just be thankful for, but will actually treasure. If nothing else, think of what this means in terms of addressing your weaknesses. Being an industrial designer means that you will often roll out products that will be greatly beneficial to everyone, making sure that whatever misunderstanding about your character exists is immediately lifted.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>That besides, it’s another job that actually encourages efficiency at all times. When it comes to designing something that’s meant to be mass-produced, you cannot afford to be too overzealous about it. Every feature the object in question has needs to be just right in order to make sure that it’s not only worth consuming, but also producing in large quantities.</p>
          <p>All in all, this job is one way to put your innovative skills to the test. Many products of industrial design continue to be useful in today’s day and age due in part because these products just work-- not too shabby, yet not too highfalutin. This is your chance to contribute to this part of humanity’s zeitgeist.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
