<div id="step5">
  <section class="individual bg-grad text-left pb-5 pt-5">
    <img src="../assets/images/indivi-bg.png" class="nebula-animation">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 id="heading">Unfortunately, Not All Is <span class="text-orange">Smooth-sailing For The Magnanimous Creator,</span> <span class="username"></span>... These Are The Shortcomings You Must Look Out For.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/smooth-sailing.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>This portion of your Archetypal Introduction does not seek to scare you... But it's best that you be made aware of the potential challenges that lie ahead of you - or perhaps you've encountered some of these challenges already.</p>
              <p>With creation comes the inevitable fact that some people are going to misunderstand you. This is inevitable because creation is linked to your own personal identity. With this in mind, it’s therefore understandable that certain social groups may not seem so welcoming to you and that people in the workplace may not initially understand the <span class="text-orange">brilliance behind the mind</span>.</p>
              <p>As such, it can be saddening to live as a Creator, to the point where you often get into arguments with other people over the fact that your idea of creativity is never really conventional. This unconventionality, therefore, brings forth certain points of friction that can prove devastating to a relationship.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>However, there is a flipside to this weakness. Although misunderstanding can be rough to handle, it does mean that you have the opportunity to enhance your stock among your colleagues and friends. Due to your unconventional and yet wise input, you are able to view things in ways that they can’t imagine. If you are able to marshal this skill and bring it to bear inside and outside of work, there is no doubt that you can overcome even the hardest of misunderstandings.</p>
          <p>Loneliness is another constant problem of the Creator, and this is often because of two things: you might, for example, space out in a conversation or situation to the point where you end up living in your own world and then regret it much later. However, it might also be due to the <span class="text-orange">intimidation that people might feel about your abilities</span>.</p>
          <p>On the one hand, this is due to the fact that you have an introverted nature. As a Creator, you often have a lot of things on your mind, and you are just waiting for the right opportunity to see your thoughts take fruit. Unfortunately, there’s often such a long time between the thought and the execution that you often tend to fantasize about what might happen next. This can either be in a romantic or an intellectual sense and when you are in this state of total wanting, you may become too lonely.</p>
          <p>On the other hand, this natural productivity of your mind can <span class="text-orange">attract feelings of negativity</span>. The fact that they are not able to reach your level can make them feel bad about themselves. This then deters them from talking to you. In a way, it could be said that this is your greatest challenge since the cure basically relies on just how well you can make them understand you. Address this problem, and loneliness will go away.</p>
          <p>Add to that, another attribute that a Creator would have is their tendency to have opinions on all kinds of things. Your mind tends to love wandering around and exploring topics, and as such, you may well be one of the only people in your social group who rarely runs out of things to say. To you, everything is fair game: political affairs, fandoms, or even how people should conduct themselves.</p>
          <p>However, this could also be a weakness in that you may have a tendency to completely derail or otherwise sour a conversation. The fact is that sometimes, while it is productive to discourse with friends, there are times where it is wiser to simply say nothing, especially since doing so may sometimes rub people off the wrong way. They might, for example, become too stressed to state their opinions on matters in front of you because you could hijack a conversation and turn it into a critiquing of your friends.</p>
          <p>In this regard, therefore, it is helpful to note that conversations should not just be a one-way street. When people have their opinions and you aren’t able to agree with them, you may still express your disagreement, but you should always be prepared to agree to disagree, because sometimes, it’s okay to leave things as they are.</p>
          <p>To be cautious is a good thing for Creators, since it’s the one thing that allows them to <span class="text-orange">regulate their own desire for overexpansion</span>. However, they may also be crippled with such insecurity and uncertainty in themselves that they become too cautious about what they do. When this happens, it may seem impossible to even try to get anything done, and your morale might drop the more people outdo or surpass you.</p>
          <p>Such unfortunate spiral can manifest itself in multiple ways. At work, for example, you may be given enough creative freedom to start something yourself, but because you’re too doubtful, you may end up only sticking to what works and never really feeling all that fulfilled on an emotional level.</p>
          <p>This lack of fulfillment can further be compounded by the fact that other people of other archetypes may end up pitching your idea due to the certainty they feel about themselves. This can certainly break your inner morale.</p>
          <p>Thus, it is imperative for you to deal with your own uncertainty. One thing you can try is for you to simply do what your heart tells you. The beautiful thing about Creators is that the more they often doubt themselves, the more capable they actually are. When you are unsure, do something anyway, and use your insecurity instead to make sure everything goes perfectly. That way, you will succeed.</p>
          <p>Now, hearing about your weaknesses may seem disheartening. But fear not, <span class="username"></span>, for there is a larger purpose for you that’s at play here...</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

